; Income-statement SECTIONS and GROUPS: a tagged SaaS book that exercises all
; seven `issection:` codes, the full subtotal ladder, a mixed `other`, and an
; `isgroup:` that merges two unrelated accounts onto one line.
;
; `fixtures/sample.journal` cannot test any of this: it carries no `issection:`
; tag at all, so it only ever produces the SIMPLE two-box statement (which is
; exactly what it is there to pin). This file is the other half.
;
; Two full calendar years, so `compare=previous` over 2026 lands exactly on 2025
; (`prior_to = from − 1 day`, `prior_from = prior_to − (to − from)`), and so the
; union merge has something to merge:
;
;   - income:grants ............ 2025 AND 2026   (a line in both columns)
;   - expenses:lawsuit ......... 2026 only       (prior reads zero)
;   - expenses:marketing:events  2025 only       (current reads zero)
;
; Section resolution, one account per rule:
;
;   1. own `issection:` .............. cogs, expenses:rent, expenses:interest, …
;   2. ancestor's `issection:` ....... expenses:salaries:eng inherits `opex`
;                                      expenses:taxes:federal inherits `tax`
;   3. type R with no tag ............ (none here — sample.journal covers it)
;   4. type X with no tag ............ (ditto)
;
; Group resolution:
;
;   - `isgroup:` tag ......... cogs:hosting → "Cloud hosting"
;   - MERGED by tag .......... expenses:marketing:ads + expenses:salaries:sales
;                              → "Growth" (two unrelated accounts, one line)
;   - shared-prefix fallback . opex members share `expenses` and the shortest
;                              (`expenses:rent`) has two segments, so the index
;                              is min(1, 1) = 1 → "Salaries", "Rent", "Marketing"
;   - shared-prefix, no root . `other` holds `income:grants` and
;                              `expenses:lawsuit`, which share NOTHING, so the
;                              index is min(0, 1) = 0 → "Income", "Expenses".
;                              Ugly on purpose: it is the third row of the plan's
;                              table, and the rule has to be total.
;
; Ground truth — every figure below was read off hledger 1.52, never off our own
; output, and the commands are quoted in tests/income_statement_grouped.rs:
;
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/is-sections.journal is -b 2026-01-01 -e 2027-01-01
;       Revenues $155,000.00   Expenses $146,700.00   Net $8,300.00
;   $ hledger -f fixtures/reports/is-sections.journal is -b 2025-01-01 -e 2026-01-01
;       Revenues $112,000.00   Expenses $116,300.00   Net $-4,300.00
;
; `hledger check` passes: every account is declared and every entry balances.
; hledger itself ignores `issection:`/`isgroup:` — they are Ledgeline tags — so
; its Revenues/Expenses split is the TYPE split, and the seven boxes are checked
; against `hledger bal` queries per account instead.

account assets:bank                  ; type: C
account equity:opening               ; type: E

; ---- revenue ----
account revenue                      ; type: R, issection: revenue
account revenue:subscriptions        ; type: R
account revenue:services             ; type: R

; ---- cost of revenue ----
; The `issection:` on the root inherits down; each child names its own line.
account cogs                         ; type: X, issection: cogs
account cogs:hosting                 ; type: X, isgroup: Cloud hosting
account cogs:payments                ; type: X, isgroup: Payment processing

; ---- operating expenses ----
account expenses:salaries            ; type: X, issection: opex
account expenses:salaries:eng        ; type: X
account expenses:salaries:sales      ; type: X, isgroup: Growth
account expenses:marketing           ; type: X, issection: opex
account expenses:marketing:ads       ; type: X, isgroup: Growth
account expenses:marketing:events    ; type: X
account expenses:rent                ; type: X, issection: opex

; ---- the three boxes that only exist because they are tagged ----
account expenses:depreciation        ; type: X, issection: depreciation
account expenses:interest            ; type: X, issection: interest
account expenses:taxes               ; type: X, issection: tax
account expenses:taxes:federal       ; type: X
account expenses:taxes:state         ; type: X

; ---- the mixed box: a revenue-type and an expense-type account together ----
account income:grants                ; type: R, issection: other
account expenses:lawsuit             ; type: X, issection: other

commodity $1,000.00

; ---------- 2024: opening only, so the 2025 window has a clean start ----------

2024-12-31 * Opening balance
    assets:bank                $50,000.00
    equity:opening

; ---------- 2025 (the PRIOR window for a 2026 report) ----------

2025-03-31 * Customers | subscription revenue
    assets:bank                $90,000.00
    revenue:subscriptions

2025-03-31 * Customers | professional services
    assets:bank                $20,000.00
    revenue:services

2025-04-30 * Cloud | hosting
    cogs:hosting               $15,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-04-30 * Stripe | processing fees
    cogs:payments               $3,300.00
    assets:bank

2025-06-30 * Payroll | engineering
    expenses:salaries:eng      $50,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-06-30 * Payroll | sales
    expenses:salaries:sales    $15,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-07-31 * Adwords | campaigns
    expenses:marketing:ads      $8,000.00
    assets:bank

; Present in 2025 and NOT in 2026 — the "Marketing" line must still appear, with
; a zero in the current column.
2025-08-31 * Conference | booth
    expenses:marketing:events   $4,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-09-30 * Landlord | office rent
    expenses:rent               $9,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-10-31 * Depreciation | equipment
    expenses:depreciation       $6,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-11-30 * Bank | loan interest
    expenses:interest           $3,500.00
    assets:bank

2025-12-31 * Innovation agency | research grant
    assets:bank                 $2,000.00
    income:grants

2025-12-31 * IRS | federal income tax
    expenses:taxes:federal      $2,000.00
    assets:bank

2025-12-31 * State | state income tax
    expenses:taxes:state          $500.00
    assets:bank

; ---------- 2026 (the reported window) ----------

2026-03-31 * Customers | subscription revenue
    assets:bank               $120,000.00
    revenue:subscriptions

2026-03-31 * Customers | professional services
    assets:bank                $30,000.00
    revenue:services

2026-04-30 * Cloud | hosting
    cogs:hosting               $18,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-04-30 * Stripe | processing fees
    cogs:payments               $4,500.00
    assets:bank

2026-06-30 * Payroll | engineering
    expenses:salaries:eng      $60,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-06-30 * Payroll | sales
    expenses:salaries:sales    $20,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-07-31 * Adwords | campaigns
    expenses:marketing:ads     $12,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-09-30 * Landlord | office rent
    expenses:rent               $9,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-10-31 * Depreciation | equipment
    expenses:depreciation       $6,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-11-30 * Bank | loan interest
    expenses:interest           $3,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-12-01 * Innovation agency | research grant
    assets:bank                 $5,000.00
    income:grants

; The other half of the mixed box, and 2026-only: `other` nets to a LOSS here
; ($5,000 of grants against an $8,000 settlement), which is the case that makes
; the box signed rather than a positive magnitude.
2026-12-01 * Settlement | patent suit
    expenses:lawsuit            $8,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-12-31 * IRS | federal income tax
    expenses:taxes:federal      $5,000.00
    assets:bank

2026-12-31 * State | state income tax
    expenses:taxes:state        $1,200.00
    assets:bank
